course: dictionary
lesson: 53
title: Accurately: exactly right
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Accurately means in a way that is exactly correct, with no mistakes. The little ending -ly turns accurate into a word that tells you how something is done. Accurate is the adjective (an accurate measure), and accurately is the adverb (measure accurately).
explain: «The mathematician worked out the value of pi very accurately.» Very tells you how exact the answer was, and the sentence is about getting the value right. So accurately must mean exactly correct. Check it by swapping in a meaning: "worked out the value of pi very exactly, with no mistakes" still makes sense.
explain: «In a study, college basketball players who slept longer shot free throws more accurately.» Shot... more accurately means they hit the target more exactly. Accurately can also mean reaching exactly the right point, not just being correct on paper.
fact: Accurately means in an exactly correct way, without mistakes.
fact: Accurately also means hitting or reaching exactly the right point.
fact: More accurately is the comparison: it means more exactly correct than before.
fact: «Accurately» is used with verbs like measure, copy, draw and throw: you measure accurately, you copy numbers accurately, you throw accurately.
fact: Phrase: «to put it accurately» means to say something in the most exact, correct way.
exercise: «The mathematician worked out the value of pi very accurately.» What does accurately mean here? | Loudly and proudly | *Exactly correct, with no mistakes | Slowly, with a long pause | Quickly and carelessly
exercise: «Players who slept longer shot free throws more accurately.» What does more accurately mean? | Running faster around the court | Shouting louder at the referee | Sleeping for longer in a bed | *Hitting the target more exactly
exercise: In maths you must copy the numbers ____ so that your answer is right. Which word fits? | loudly | happily | *accurately | quickly
test: In science you must measure the length of the plant ____ with a ruler. Which word fits best? | carelessly | sadly | *accurately | noisily
test: «To put it accurately, the bridge was built in 1890.» What does «to put it accurately» mean? | To say it as loudly as possible | To say it in a secret language | To say it without thinking | *To say it in the most exact, correct way
exam: «The archer hit the centre of the target accurately, and the judge checked every measurement.» Which word means exactly correct? | centre | *accurately | archer | judge
